Z||000021||WKDFIRO||08-16-2001||08:51 PM||||I feel like I have to stand up for the very least the south western portion of California! There are Fieros out here, just not a whole lot of them on the street anymore. I drive mine daily and see a few now and again but the numbers are definitely dwindling.  When it comes to a club functions though, the Fieros I do see coming out are easily some of the best on the west coast.<P>So I can forgive some of them for preserving their ride.<P>We are here, some of us just don't like showing off too much!||||reg||6
Z||000022||mrfiero||08-16-2001||09:08 PM||||You just missed me......I drove my '88 GT T-Top from Denver to Vegas (then onto L.A & San Jose).  I was in Vegas Sunday afternoon and again on Tuesday night.<P>If you think 110* is hot, try driving through the Mojave desert in a T-Top GT with no AC!!  VERY hot!  I'm still sunburnt from that one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Voytek||08-17-2001||10:36 AM||||I feel for you, mrfiero.  That is exactly why I spent $600 CDN on fixing my A/C before we left.  It was worth every penny.  We had the sunroof out for a bit too but had to put it back in.<P>I guess it's true that more and more people don't drive their nice Fieros as much in order to preserve them.  Of'course, there's the fact that Fieros are definitely in decline.||||reg||1
